### security guidelines
- **Validate buffer size before writing**: Ensure `buf_size >= 10` before writing to the first and last 10 bytes. If not, return `NULL` to prevent out-of-bounds writes.  
  *Example:*  
  ```c
  if (buf_size < 10) { return NULL; }
  ```
- **Bound-check loops**: Limit the first loop to `i < buf_size` and the last loop to `i < buf_size - 10 + 10` (i.e., `i < buf_size`). This ensures writes stay within allocated memory.  
  *Example:*  
  ```c
  for (size_t i = 0; i < 10 && i < buf_size; i++) { buf[i] = 'A'; }
  for (size_t i = buf_size - 10; i < buf_size; i++) { buf[i] = 'A'; }
